-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the electron pair on the network
-- two equal spins j coupled to J: exchanging them multiplies the coupled state by (−1)^(2j − J), so it is
-- odd exactly when 2j − J is odd (doubled spins tj, tJ). The coefficients of chem/spin.cub show it below.
spin-pair-odd : Nat → Nat → Bool
spin-pair-odd tj tJ = odd (nat-half (monus (plus tj tj) tJ))
